speechtext:
In view of the statements made by the hon. gentleman on previous occasions, and in view of the urgent necessity of having a dredge in the lower provinces I did look into this matter. I may say to the hon. gentleman that he will be fully responsible
for the conduct of the department, for the reason that there has been no change made at Ottawa and neither has there been any change made at Sorel. The supervision is the same now as it was before. If there is any correspondence in the department to which he refers between any of the officials,
I wish he would give me the names because I am giving the information to the House and to him as it is given to me by the chief officers of the department. There has been no change made whatever; no change in the instructions; no change in the supervision, and so far as I am personally concerned any action that I have taken and any intimation I have given has been in the direction of urging that all speed be made towards carrying out this work. I have no information from any of the officers of the department or from any source, that there has been any change made whatever. The only personal action I took was to urge on the officers the necessity of having this dredge completed as quickly as possible.
